# Accepted exceptions for `trivy config infra/project`
#
# Scope: a static project website on S3 + CloudFront. The bucket holds only
# public build output; there is no form, API, or datastore behind the origin.

# AWS-0132: site bucket uses SSE-S3 rather than a customer managed key.
# The objects are public website files served to anyone, so a CMK protects
# content that is already published. It would also add a KMS decrypt on every
# CloudFront origin fetch. Same key-governance scope accepted in eks-secure.
AWS-0132

# AWS-0011: no WAF in front of the distribution.
# The origin is a private bucket of static assets reachable only over OAC:
# no query handling, no forms, no credentials to steal. WAF's base and
# per-request cost buys no meaningful control for read-only public files.
# Revisit if the site ever gains a dynamic endpoint.
AWS-0011
